# Source archives (github.com/<owner>/<repo>/archive/...) are `git archive`
# output, which honours export-ignore. Everything except the release directory
# threat-models-for-aws-services/, README.md and LICENSE is repository
# scaffolding and stays out of the archive, so an archive of a tag is the
# release itself plus the README and licence. Patterns are anchored to the
# repository root.
/.github export-ignore
/docs export-ignore
/CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md export-ignore
/.gitignore export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
